NITREWRITTEN - Third-party licenses
====================================

NITREWRITTEN bundles or can use the third-party components listed below.
Each entry notes what the component is used for and its license.

- 7-Zip (bundled; archive extraction)
    Used by NITREWRITTEN to extract .7z/.zip/.rar and other archives.
    Homepage: https://www.7-zip.org/
    License: GNU LGPL (main), BSD 3-clause and BSD 2-clause for parts of the code.
    The full license text shipped with the bundled 7-Zip files follows
    (verbatim copy of resources/tools/License.txt):

- unRAR (optional; NOT bundled)
    Used only if present on the system, to extract .rar archives.
    NITREWRITTEN invokes the external unrar/unar/bsdtar command-line tools;
    no unRAR code is distributed with this project.

- FFmpeg (optional; NOT bundled)
    Used only if present on the system, to convert BIK movies to WBM
    (Enhanced Edition). NITREWRITTEN invokes the external ffmpeg binary;
    no FFmpeg code is distributed with this project.

- Neverwinter Vault (online catalog)
    Project catalog and images shown in the Vault tab are fetched from
    https://neverwintervault.org/ at runtime. No Vault content is bundled.

- NIT - Neverwinter Nights Mod Installer Tool (inspiration)
    NITREWRITTEN was inspired by NIT by Surazal.
    https://neverwintervault.org/project/nwn1/other/tool/neverwinter-nights-mod-installer-tool-nit
    NIT is a separate project by its own author; NITREWRITTEN is an
    independent rewrite and shares no code with it.

- Neverwinter Nights
    Neverwinter Nights is a trademark of Wizards of the Coast.
    NITREWRITTEN is not affiliated with Beamdog, Bioware or Wizards of the Coast.


